"<div data-type=\"panel-success\"><p><strong>WHAT PASSED</strong>: everything that passed is listed in this comment. What is still to be fixed is in the next comment below.</p></div>\n<p>Tested on the QA branch <a href=\"https://sv12048.qa.shopview.com\">sv12048</a> (build v26.45.0-747429d) and compared with production (build v26.45.1-753355c) on 5 Nov 2026. I went through every item in the Powertools test plan and Chris's rules from his comment of 3 Nov.</p>\n<p>A work order booked for the whole work order now picks up lines that are approved after it was booked, and the shift's technician is added to them. On production the shift keeps only the lines it was booked with.</p>\n<h3>Before and after</h3>\n<figure data-type=\"media-single\" data-layout=\"center\" data-width=\"100\" data-width-type=\"percentage\"><div data-type=\"media\" data-media-type=\"file\" data-id=\"0c314f09-1ac6-4ceb-a590-bba1022c1788\" data-collection=\"upload-user-collection-1343233018\" data-alt=\"before-after-shift-lines.png\"></div></figure>\n<p><em>Picture 1: Left and middle, production: work order S2-1931 was booked as \"Entire work order\" with 2 lines, then line 3 was approved. Its shift still shows 2 lines. Right, QA branch: work order S12048-17582 was booked the same way with 2 lines, and lines 3 and 4 approved later both joined the shift (\"4 lines \u00b7 Est. 8h\").</em></p>\n<h3>What was checked</h3>\n<table><tbody>\n<tr><th>#</th><th>Check</th><th>Result</th><th>Status</th></tr>\n<tr><td>A</td><td>Work order created from a Schedule cell</td><td>Empty spot on Marissa Armstrong's lane (Fri 6 Nov) &gt; New Work Order &gt; customer and asset &gt; Save. The dialog closed, I stayed on the Schedule and the block appeared (S12048-17601). Opening the block showed \"0 lines\". After approving 2 lines on the Lines tab it showed \"2 lines \u00b7 Est. 4h\", and the technician was on both lines.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>B</td><td>\"Entire work order\" picks up lines approved later</td><td>S12048-17582: booked with 2 lines. Line 3 approved: shift shows 3, technician on line 3. Line 4 left waiting: shift stays at 3. Line 4 approved: shift shows 4.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>C</td><td>\"Choose lines\" never grows</td><td>Both lines ticked (S12048-17584) and 1 of 2 ticked (S12048-17583). A line approved later did not join either shift and stays in the sidebar as unscheduled.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>D</td><td>Single-line drops</td><td>Work order card with one line (S12048-17585): booked with no dialog, a line approved later joins. One line dragged from the line panel (S12048-17586): a line approved later does not join.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>E</td><td>Multi-day bookings</td><td>3 lines \u00d7 6h booked over Fri and Sat (S12048-17587). A new line approved: both days show it and keep the same hours. With \"Choose lines\" (S12048-17588) neither day gains it.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>F</td><td>Other ways of booking</td><td>Assign Work Order from an empty cell (S12048-17589): a line approved later joins and the technician is added. Card dropped on the SERVICE department row (S12048-17590): the line joins with no technician added. Moved from the department row onto David Haynes: the next approved line joins with him on it. A single line parked on the department row and moved to a technician (S12048-17591) still does not grow.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>G</td><td>Ended and existing shifts don't change</td><td>S12048-17593 booked yesterday and tomorrow: a new line joined tomorrow's shift only. A shift booked before this build (S2-17562) did not pick up a new line.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>H</td><td>Un-completing a line</td><td>S12048-17594: line completed, then right-click &gt; Uncomplete. The shift stayed the same (2 lines) and the technician was not added twice. The first step of this check is a question in the next comment.</td><td>PASSED (see next comment)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>I</td><td>Deleting shifts cleans up technicians</td><td>Delete this shift (S12048-17585): technician removed from the lines. 3-day booking (S12048-17596), middle day &gt; \"This and all later shifts\": later days gone, technician stays on the lines. Remaining day deleted: technician removed, another technician's shift on the same work order keeps its technician.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>J1</td><td>Undo after deleting a whole-work-order shift</td><td>S12048-17589: delete, Undo, shift back with 3 lines. A new line approved afterwards joins.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>J2</td><td>Undo after deleting a chosen-lines shift</td><td>S12048-17584: delete, Undo, shift back. A new line approved afterwards does not join.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>K</td><td>Lead technician change with \"Clear shifts\" + Undo</td><td>S12048-17599: Board View card \u22ee &gt; Reassign lead technician &gt; \"Clear \u2026's scheduled shifts?\" &gt; Clear shifts. Shift removed. Undo: shift back, and a line approved afterwards joins it.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>L1</td><td>Decline a line on a shift</td><td>S12048-17600: right-click &gt; Decline. The line stays on the shift, shown \"Auth Declined\".</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>L2</td><td>Delete a line on a shift</td><td>S12048-17600: right-click &gt; Delete line &gt; Delete. The line left the shift (3 lines became 2).</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>L3</td><td>No error toasts, no broken Schedule</td><td>None seen in any of the checks above.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>R1</td><td>Approving several lines at once</td><td>S12048-17601: 2 waiting lines ticked &gt; \"Approve (2)\". Both joined the shift with the technician on them. Shift length unchanged.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CW3</td><td>Shift already under way (Chris, answer 3)</td><td>S12048-17603 booked today 9 AM\u20131 PM. A line approved at 10:56 AM joined the shift and the technician was added.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CW5</td><td>Technician limit per line (Chris, answer 5)</td><td>Edit Labor allows \"Max 5 selections\". A waiting line with 5 technicians approved onto Marissa Armstrong's shift (S12048-17604): the line keeps its 5, she is not added. Dragging a line that already has 5 (S12048-17605) gives the same result, so approval follows the drag rule.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CW6</td><td>Line sent back for approval (Chris, answer 6)</td><td>S12048-17603: right-click &gt; Authorization required. The line stays on the shift, shown \"Auth Req'd\".</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CW</td><td>Shift length</td><td>In every check above a new line never made a shift longer.</td><td>PASSED</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<figure data-type=\"media-single\" data-layout=\"center\" data-width=\"100\" data-width-type=\"percentage\"><div data-type=\"media\" data-media-type=\"file\" data-id=\"496826a7-4bd0-41ed-8016-80412e357654\" data-collection=\"upload-user-collection-1343233018\" data-alt=\"branch-new-wo-from-schedule.png\"></div></figure>\n<p><em>Picture 2: QA branch, check A. New Work Order from an empty spot on the Schedule, the block right after Save (0 lines), and the same block after approving lines on the Lines tab (2 one by one, 2 with \"Approve (2)\").</em></p>\n<figure data-type=\"media-single\" data-layout=\"center\" data-width=\"100\" data-width-type=\"percentage\"><div data-type=\"media\" data-media-type=\"file\" data-id=\"8db38a43-7d07-4d65-af5e-2acc69ab83dc\" data-collection=\"upload-user-collection-1343233018\" data-alt=\"branch-decline-delete.png\"></div></figure>\n<p><em>Picture 3: QA branch, checks L1 and L2. The declined line stays on the shift as \"Auth Declined\". The deleted line is gone (3 lines became 2).</em></p>\n"
